  "query_preview": "(Friday through Monday)...\nSlow warming of high temperatures will continue for inland areas\nthrough Saturday with high temperatures on Saturday ranging from\nthe mid 70s to lower 80s near the coast to the mid 90s to 105 for\nthe Inland Empire with 112 to 116 for the lower deserts. \n\nFor Sunday and Monday, high pressure will begin to slowly weaken\nwith the flow aloft becoming more southeasterly. This would allow\nfor some additional influx of monsoonal moisture into the area.\nHigh temperatures for Monday of next week would be within a few\ndegrees of average for the coast, valleys, and mountains and a \nfew degrees above average for the deserts. Low temperatures would \nbe a few degrees above average for the coast and valleys and 5 to \n10 degrees above average for the mountains and deserts.\n\nHigh temperatures for next Monday would range from the mid to\nupper 70s near the coast to the 90s for the Inland Empire with 106\nto 110 for the lower deserts. There will also be a slight chance\nof showers and thunderstorms for the mountains for Sunday\nafternoon and Monday afternoon.",
